# Leaks LeakSanitizer reports that are not in Dicolens. Each says whose it is
# and why it is let through. A leak with any frame of Dicolens' own in its
# stack matches nothing here.

# fcitx5-qt, the desktop's input method plugin, which Qt loads into the
# tests when QT_IM_MODULE names it (it does on Omarchy; in CI's container
# there is no fcitx). The first key a test presses makes its candidate
# window, with a theme and a file watcher that the plugin keeps until the
# process ends and never frees.
leak:fcitx::

# The reference count Qt hangs on a socket notifier the first time it fires,
# here the one fcitx5-qt listens to its daemon with. It goes when the
# notifier does, which is with the plugin above: never. (A notifier leaked
# by Dicolens would be reported itself, from where it was made, not here.)
leak:QSocketNotifier::event
